Z||000000||JetroGT||02-08-2000||05:49 AM||||I may have to move to Texas! On one hand it would be good because my fiero wouldt never see Wisconsin snow again, and on the other hand no more Dells Run. No more going on fall cruses to Door county on the Fall color tour. Plus I just renewed my membership with NIFE and the Fiero Fanitics. <BR>The company wants to move me to the Dallis, Fort Worth area. I just got hit with this news tonight, and I have 7 days to decide. And if I do move I better get my air recharged!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||11
Z||000001||william_thorniii||02-08-2000||05:44 PM||||Jetro,<P>Bummer.  I know how you feel.  I live in Dayton, OH and last year the company told me I had 24 hours to decide about moving to FDL, WI and have a future with the company or stay here and get fired after a while.  I made my decision to move up to the blistery North.  A few weeks later I was informed that a place up North would not be available for me.  I took that to be a pink slip in disguise.  So far, 8 months later, I still have my job down here.  Who cares about long term anyway?  Just wait it out, and don't worry about things that might happen.  It is not definite until you un-pack the truck.  <P>Not to mention that I would easily give up the Dells for getting several more months of summer.  Think about all the wonderful days you will have to drive your baby and not worry about salt/sand/snow.  Also if you are into old Detroit Iron, everybody knows that AZ, TX, OK have the best there is to offer since there is no salt put down.  Also last I heard TX allows both concealed weapons and the consumption of alcohol while operating a motor vehicle.  That sounds like my kind of state.  Although you must remember the famous quote "Ain't nothin' from Texas 'cept steers and queers, and I don't see no horns on you!"<P>TX guys, please don't flame me for quoting a movie... THX, <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
