Z||000009||William Federle||02-12-2000||07:44 AM||||Go West young man! I spent a few months in Texas in the DFW area in the 70's and again in the 80's. I could definitely live there. It does get cold once in a while but not for long and not as cold. I've been there in the summer when it was 100 deg. F and it felt good - it wouldn't up here in Milwaukee. And the people are friendly. Here in Wis. sometimes I think they're wired too tight in the winter (I get like that too).<p>[This message has been edited by William Federle (edited 02-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||batboy||02-12-2000||09:38 AM||||I'm confused! Al got irritated about a reference to illegal immigrants and said they were "his people" so does that mean Al's an illegal immigrant too? I think <B>illegal</B> is the key word here regardless of their race, creed, or what country they're originally from. Most of us Americans agree that somewhere along the lines, our ancestors were immigrants, but none of mine immigrated illegally. I think illegal aliens (regardless of their nationality) create a lot of economic and social problems in the U.S. I resent having to pay taxes to support these <B>illegals</B> and hate to see them taking jobs away from law-biding American citizens (whether they were born here or immigrated here legally).<P>I didn't see one reference to "minorities" in Wisconsin's statement, yet it was automatically assumed he was talking about minorities. I have lots of friends that are minorities, but none of them are illegal immigrants. What about women with breast implants. He mentioned them too. How come nobody got mad about his comment about fake titties?. <I>How dare you make fun of silcone babes!</I> JEEZ! I think we are getting a little too touchy here. Nuff said!<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 02-12-2000).]||||reg||1
